        <body>
            
            <div type="edition" xml:lang="nld-Latn" rendition="class:latin maturity:undetermined">
                
                <p>
                    <lb n="1"/>HIER LEYT <expan><abbr>BEGRAV</abbr><ex>EN</ex></expan> DEN
                    <lb n="2"/>EERSAMEN REYNIER <expan><abbr>VA</abbr><ex>N</ex></expan>
                    <lb n="3"/>BUYTENDYCK VAN DORT                   
                    <lb n="4"/>IN SYN LEVEN <expan><abbr>COOPM</abbr><ex>AN</ex></expan>
                    <lb n="5"/>EN GUARNISOENBOEK
                    <lb n="6" break="no"/>HOUDER DER STADT
                    <lb n="7"/>NAGAPATNAM IN DEN
                    <lb n="8"/>HEERE ONTSLAPEN DEN
                    <lb n="9"/><hi rend="check">II=</hi> MEY <hi rend="check">A=</hi> 1684 OUDT
                    <lb n="10"/>SYNDE OMTRENT 64
                    <lb n="11"/>IAREN
                </p>
                
            </div>	
            
            <div type="apparatus">
                <listApp>
                    <app loc="5">
                        <lem source="bib:Cotton1946_01">°BOEK°</lem>
                        <rdg source="bib:Mārkciyakānti+al2007_01">°BOEH°</rdg>
                    </app>
                    <app loc="9">
                        <lem source="bib:Mārkciyakānti+al2007_01"><hi rend="check">II=</hi></lem>
                        <rdg source="bib:Cotton1946_01">V<hi rend="superscript">N</hi></rdg>
                    </app>
                    <app loc="9">
                        <lem source="bib:Mārkciyakānti+al2007_01"><hi rend="check">A=</hi></lem>
                        <rdg source="bib:Cotton1946_01">A<hi rend="superscript">O</hi></rdg>
                    </app>
                    <app loc="9">
                        <lem source="bib:Cotton1946_01">OUDT</lem>
                        <rdg source="bib:Mārkciyakānti+al2007_01">OUCT</rdg>
                    </app>
                </listApp>
            </div>
            
            <div type="translation" resp="part:emfr">
                <p n="1-7">
                    Here lies buried the worthy Reijnier van Buytendijck van Dort,<note><bibl><ptr target="bib:Cotton1946_01"/></bibl>: <quote>Dort is an abbreviation for Dordrecht.</quote></note>
                    in his life 
                    merchant 
                    and accountant <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>boekhouder</foreign></supplied> of the garnison in the city of Nagapatnam,
                    who passed away in the Lord
                    on 2 May of the year 1684, 
                    being approximately 64 years old.                   
                </p>       
            </div>	
            
            <div type="commentary">
                <p n="1"><foreign>DEN</foreign>. This dative/accusative form is surprisingly used where a nominative is obviously required.</p>
                </div>
            
